<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Chausa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1539">1539</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Chausa was fought in June 1539 near Chausa on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>, where the Afghan leader Sher Khan surprised and routed the army of the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humayun">Humayun</a>. Humayun barely escaped by swimming the river. The victory let Sher Khan proclaim himself Sher Shah, and after a second victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> in 1540 he drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-chausa.jpg" alt="Battle of Chausa" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Beylarbey · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_plan_of_Chausa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
